Confidence-Indexed Hierarchical Probabilistic Consequence Graphs

A Mathematical Theory of Recursive Decision Dynamics

Author: Ouadi Maakoul

AI: chatGpt, Claude, Deepseek, Meta 

Abstract

Decision-making in complex socio-technical systems is fundamentally constrained by uncertainty, incomplete information, and the recursive propagation of consequences across interconnected domains. Existing decision-support frameworks typically optimise expected utility or forecast future system states but seldom provide a unified mathematical representation coupling uncertainty, confidence, and recursive consequence propagation.

This dissertation proposes the Confidence-Indexed Hierarchical Probabilistic Consequence Graph (CI‑HPCG) framework—a mathematical model in which every decision induces a dynamically evolving directed consequence graph whose nodes encode probabilistic impacts, temporal evolution, and confidence measures derived from Bayesian decision theory. Confidence is defined through posterior regret rather than as a heuristic score, establishing a direct connection between uncertainty quantification and optimal decision theory.

The dissertation develops a sequence of definitions, operators, and convergence theorems governing the evolution of consequence graphs. Under bounded branching conditions and exponentially discounted impact propagation, the aggregate consequence functional is shown to converge absolutely. The confidence process itself is proved to converge almost surely under weak conditions (Theorem 3.3), while stability of the recommended action is shown to require a strictly stronger, separately identified condition (Theorem 3.4)—a distinction the dissertation treats as a substantive finding rather than a gap to be smoothed over.

The proposed framework is a mathematical foundation for high-assurance decision-support systems, not a complete implementation. No empirical validation, simulation, or computational experiment is claimed anywhere in this document; all results are analytic and their scope is stated exactly.

